.TH SETUID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setuid \- sets user ids according to linux credential and privilege rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int setuid(uid_t user);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets user IDs according to Linux credential and privilege rules. This is a direct per-thread syscall.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setuid (2)
